{"school":{"dbn":"32K384","name":"P.S. /I.S. 384 Frances E. Carter","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"32","district_label":"District 32","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":343,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"242 COOPER STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11207","phone":"718-246-6500","website":"www.fec384.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/73530","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"Students at PS/IS 384 often say that the school feels like a part of their family. As a 3K - 8th grade school, many students have spent nine years or more in our building, and have truly become part of our family. Our school is a place where all students are held to high expectations, and are pushed to be the best they can be. Our students understand that hard work always pays off, and we ensure that all students are challenged. We have a Dual Language program so that students can become fluent in both Spanish and English.  We are a \"Kids at Hope\" school, a place in which all teachers, staff and community members believe that all children can achieve success, no exceptions. In a caring, warm school environment, our students are comfortable taking risks. Our students go on many wonderful trips around NYC to visit the Statue of Liberty, attend a Major League Baseball game, or take a walking tour of Chinatown. Many of our classrooms are filled with interesting class pets so our students can learn about caring for animals. At PS/IS 384 we want our parents to feel supported, so the school has an open door policy, and parents are welcome to come in and speak with the principal or teachers at any time.","start_time":"08:05am","end_time":"02:25pm","languages":null,"subway":"L to Wilson Av","bus":"B20, B26, B60","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Bushwick","latitude":40.6896,"longitude":-73.9048,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"at